# Legacy operator venv for mint-dev / Ray inspection (CPU).
#
# Scope:
# - Installed into a host venv such as `/root/venv_k2_py31213`.
# - Used for operator workflows (Ray inspection, issue repro, cluster probes).
# - The API server should prefer `PFS_RUNTIME_ENV_ROOT/host-venv/bin/python` plus the
#   shared runtime env root built by `scripts/build_runtime_env.py`.
# - GPU workers still use the Mint Docker image for ABI-bound packages.
#
# Notes:
# - Must include `torch` on the driver to deserialize tensors from Ray object store.
# - Must keep `ray` version aligned with the cluster.
# - Python patch version must match the Ray cluster Python exactly (Ray is strict).
#
# Reference:
# - This file is no longer the source of truth for server runtime deps.
# - `pyproject.toml` plus `tool.mint.runtime_env` define the canonical shared runtime env.
#
# Installation note:
# - `torch==2.9.1+cpu` may require the PyTorch CPU wheel index. Example:
#   python -m pip install --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu 'torch==2.9.1+cpu'

ray[default]==2.51.1
torch==2.9.1+cpu

